<%#
  Hidden sign-in name for password managers on forms that ask for the current
  password but show no email box. Without it, managers take the next text box
  (usually the authenticator code) for the username and fill the email there.
  Pattern from Chromium's "Password Form Styles that Chromium Understands" and
  1Password's "Design your website to work best with 1Password": a username
  field with the account's value, hidden with display:none.
  The server never reads this field; it already knows the account from the
  session. Include it immediately before the password box.
%>
<input type="email" name="username" value="<%= email %>" autocomplete="username"
  class="autofill-username" readonly tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" />
